Stylus axes in units per millimeter ([Stylus] AxisResolution)

The stylus device reports 9600 x 7200 units whatever the size of the screen: 28.5 x 25.4 um per
unit on the Surface Pro 9, coarser than the pen position is known, and the resolution that is
announced with the axes is rounded to whole units per mm (35 and 39 for 35.05 and 39.43), so
lengths computed from it are off by up to 1.1 %.

With [Stylus] AxisResolution = N the axes have N units per mm, their range is the size of the
screen (27389 x 18259 for N = 100) and the announced resolution is exact. 0 (the default) keeps
9600 x 7200. The touch device is not changed.

